REFERENCE   1  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Xia QY, Wang XT, Fang R, Wang Z, Zhao M, Chen H, Chen N, Teng XD,
            Wang X, Wei X, Ye SB, Li R, Ma HH, Lu ZF, Zhou XJ and Rao Q.
  TITLE     Clinicopathologic and Molecular Analysis of the TFEB Fusion Variant
            Reveals New Members of TFEB Translocation Renal Cell Carcinomas
            (RCCs): Expanding the Genomic Spectrum
  JOURNAL   Am. J. Surg. Pathol. 44 (4), 477-489 (2020)
   PUBMED   31764220
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Report morphological features of Xp11 renal cell carcinoma
            with TFEB fusion variants.
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Slade L, Biswas D, Ihionu F, El Hiani Y, Kienesberger PC and
            Pulinilkunnil T.
  TITLE     A lysosome independent role for TFEB in activating DNA repair and
            inhibiting apoptosis in breast cancer cells
  JOURNAL   Biochem. J. 477 (1), 137-160 (2020)
   PUBMED   31820786
  REMARK    GeneRIF: The authors data provide novel evidence towards the
            involvement of TFEB in DNA damage repair induced by doxorubicin
            treatment and apoptosis regulation independent of its lysosomal
            effects in triple-negative breast cancer cells.
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Curnock R, Calcagni A, Ballabio A and Cullen PJ.
  TITLE     TFEB controls retromer expression in response to nutrient
            availability
  JOURNAL   J. Cell Biol. 218 (12), 3954-3966 (2019)
   PUBMED   31694921
  REMARK    GeneRIF: retromer expression is upregulated by transcription factor
            EB (TFEB) and other members of the MiTF/TFE family of transcription
            factors through association with CLEAR elements in the promoters of
            the retromer genes VPS35 and VPS26A
REFERENCE   4  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Gupta S, Argani P, Jungbluth AA, Chen YB, Tickoo SK, Fine SW,
            Gopalan A, Al-Ahmadie HA, Sirintrapun SJ, Sanchez A, Hakimi AA,
            Mcfarlane T, Salazar PA, Williamson SR, Skala SL, Mehra R, Hes O,
            Antonescu CR, Ladanyi M, Arcila ME and Reuter VE.
  TITLE     TFEB Expression Profiling in Renal Cell Carcinomas:
            Clinicopathologic Correlations
  JOURNAL   Am. J. Surg. Pathol. 43 (11), 1445-1461 (2019)
   PUBMED   31600176
  REMARK    GeneRIF: 6p21.1 amplified renal tumors show increased TFEB
            expression but not as much as t(6;11) tumors. Findings correlate
            with the less consistent/diffuse expression of downstream markers
            of TFEB activation (cathepsin K, melan A, HMB45) seen in the
            amplified neoplasms, suggesting that the aggressive biological
            behavior of 6p21.1 amplified renal tumors might be secondary to
            other genes at the 6p21.1 locus that are co-amplified.
REFERENCE   5  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Du J, Ren W, Yao F, Wang H, Zhang K, Luo M, Shang Y, O'Connell D,
            Bei Z, Wang H, Xiong R and Yang Y.
  TITLE     YY1 cooperates with TFEB to regulate autophagy and lysosomal
            biogenesis in melanoma
  JOURNAL   Mol. Carcinog. 58 (11), 2149-2160 (2019)
   PUBMED   31448838
  REMARK    GeneRIF: these studies identify YY1 as a novel cotranscription
            factor of TFEB in regulating autophagy and lysosomal functions and
            suggest YY1 could be a therapeutic target in cancer treatment
REFERENCE   6  (bases 1 to 2364)
  AUTHORS   Davis IJ, Hsi BL, Arroyo JD, Vargas SO, Yeh YA, Motyckova G,
            Valencia P, Perez-Atayde AR, Argani P, Ladanyi M, Fletcher JA and
            Fisher DE.
  TITLE     Cloning of an Alpha-TFEB fusion in renal tumors harboring the
            t(6;11)(p21;q13) chromosome translocation
  JOURNAL   Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. U.S.A. 100 (10), 6051-6056 (2003)
   PUBMED   12719541
  REMARK    GeneRIF: This gene fuses with an intronless gene in renal tumors
            harboring the t(6;11)(p21;q13) chromosome translocation.
